  "raw": {
    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/instructional-associate-continuing-track-department-of-biology-faculty-of-science-2/": {
      "title": "Instructional Associate, Continuing-Track, Department of Biology – Faculty of Science",
      "description": "Instructional Associate, Continuing-Track, Department of Biology – Faculty of Science | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities Instructional Associate, Continuing-Track, Department of Bio… Instructional Associate, Continuing-Track, Department of Biology – Faculty of Science The Department of Biology at Brandon University invites applications for the position of Instructional Associate with introductory emphasis in a continuing-track appointment to begin January 4, 2027, or as mutually agreed, subject to budgetary approval. The department of Biology is in a period of active growth and rejuvenation, particularly with respect to modernizing our undergraduate program. We seek an exceptional instructor with commitments to teaching excellence and pedagogical development, with that person able to adapt to a dynamic learning environment. The successful candidate will contribute to this momentum through a diverse repertoire of modern laboratory skills, and they will have outstanding skills in problem solving, communication, and organization. Responsibilities : The successful applicant will deliver in-person laboratories for up to five sections per week for 15:162 Cell, Genetics and Evolution (CGE) and 15:163 Biodiversity, Functions and Interactions (BFI), two team-taught first-year courses required by all Biology students at BU. As the CGE and BFI laboratory instructor, the successful applicant will be responsible for laboratory preparation, set-up, clean-up, laboratory safety, the preparation and marking of laboratory tests, the maintenance of laboratory records, coordination with other members of the CGE and BFI teaching teams regarding laboratory content and assessment, and the supervision of graduate students and undergraduate student assistants for marking, dishwashing, and the greenhouse. In cooperation with other departmental IAs, additional duties include ordering for laboratory classes for other Biology courses, ordering and receiving departmental supplies, maintaining and storing departmental equipment, and maintaining departmental teaching inventories. Qualifications : an M.Sc. in Biology or a related discipline is required, although a Ph.D. is preferred. Evidence of a successful record of laboratory instruction and demonstrated expertise in both traditional methods and molecular biological techniques is required. Applicants may seek to establish an experiential/traditional equivalency to the Master’s Degree and are invited to contact the Office of the Dean of Science on how to establish equivalent academic or professional credentials. Rank : Instructional Associate Salary : Commensurate with qualifications and experience. Application Deadline: October 6, 2026 or until position is filled. Start Date: January 4, 2027 Internal Applicants: Qualified internal applicants are invited to apply. Internal applicants are current full-time or part-time Brandon University Faculty Association (BUFA) Members on a continuing or regular appointment (does not include Contract Academic Staff (CAS)), CAS who hold RFR in one (1) or more courses in the Department of Biology, or the spouse/partner of a current full-time or part-time BUFA Member on a continuing or regular appointment. Internal applicants are required to identify as such in their letter of application. To Apply: Interested applicants are invited to submit an application package as one single electronic file (e.g., PDF) that must contain a letter of application (including details regarding area of specialization and experience relevant to the stated position requirements and preferences), a curriculum vitae, the names and contact information of three (3) references, statement of teaching philosophy (2 pages maximum), evidence of teaching effectiveness (course outlines, instructional material, teaching evaluations), and a statement on citizenship/Canadian immigration status to: Dr. Christophe LeMoine Dean of Science Brandon University Brandon, MB R7A 6A9 Science@BrandonU.ca We thank all applicants for their interest in applying for this position and advise that only candidates selected for interviews will be contacted. Short-listed candidates will be expected to provide copies of credentials at time of interview. Issued August 25, 2026 Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. Should you require an accommodation during any phase of the recruitment process, contact HR at hr@brandonu.ca . All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
    },
    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/francophone-studies-and-languages-3-year-term-faculty-of-arts/": {
      "title": "Top Toolbar Links",
      "description": "Francophone Studies and Languages – 3-Year Term – Faculty of Arts | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities Francophone Studies and Languages – 3-Year Term &#8211… Francophone Studies and Languages – 3-Year Term – Faculty of Arts The Department of Francophone Studies and Languages at Brandon University invites applications for a 3-year term position. The successful candidate must demonstrate a commitment to student-centered undergraduate teaching and learning and provide evidence of teaching competence in Francophone literary and cultural studies and French language instruction, including grammar courses. Preference will be given to candidates whose expertise encompasses one or more of the following areas: French and Francophone literature and culture, with expertise extending beyond Québec considered a major asset; literary and interdisciplinary critical approaches; Francophone cinema, media, and digital cultures, and intermedial practices; gender, feminist, and sexuality studies; the politics of language, identity, and culture; and comparative, transnational, intercultural, or multilingual approaches to literary and cultural studies. In addition, the successful candidate must have an active research and/or research-creation and publishing program. Willingness to participate collegially in service to the department, university and the community that it serves will be expected. Qualifications: The preferred qualification for this position is a PhD in French or Francophone Studies, or a related disciplinary or interdisciplinary field. ABD applicants nearing completion prior to the start date of the appointment may also be considered. Applicants may seek to establish an experiential/traditional equivalency to the Doctorate degree and are invited to contact the Office of the Dean of Arts on how to establish equivalent academic or professional credentials. Rank: Commensurate with qualifications and experience Salary: Commensurate with qualifications and experience. Application Deadline: September 18, 2026 or until position is filled. Start Date: January 4, 2027 Internal Applicants: Qualified internal applicants are invited to apply. Internal applicants are current full-time or part-time Brandon University Faculty Association (BUFA) Members on a continuing or regular appointment (does not include Contract Academic Staff (CAS)), CAS who hold RFR in one (1) or more courses in the Department identified in this posting, or the spouse/partner of a current full-time or part-time BUFA Member on a continuing or regular appointment. Internal applicants are required to identify as such in their letter of application. To Apply: Interested candidates should submit an application package as one single PDF document containing: Letter of Application (to include details about candidate’s area of specialization and its relevance to the stated position requirements and preferences) Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Evidence of teaching and research and/or research-creation (including course outlines and at least one sample publication relevant to this position) Name and contact information for three references Citizenship/Canadian Immigration Status Priority consideration will be given to Canadian Citizens and Permanent Residents. Please submit applications to: Dr. Gregory Kennedy Dean of Arts FSLSearch@brandonu.ca Issued August 14, 2026 Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. Should you require an accommodation during any phase of the recruitment process, contact HR at hr@brandonu.ca . All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
    },
    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/student-communications-assistant-sa-iii-faculty-of-arts/": {
      "title": "Student Communications Assistant – SA III – Faculty of Arts",
      "description": "Student Communications Assistant – SA III – Faculty of Arts | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities Student Communications Assistant – SA III – Facu… Student Communications Assistant – SA III – Faculty of Arts Applications are to be received by: 4:30 p.m. on September 17, 2026 Classification: Student Assistant III Employee Group: PSAC Job Title: Student Communications Assistant Department: Faculty of Arts Wage or Salary: $18.41/hr Number of Hours to Work: 10hrs per week Start Date: September 24, 2026 Number of Positions available: 1 End Date of Employment: December 18, 2026 Date Issued: September 2, 2026 Key Duties: 1. Create materials to assist with recruitment or orientation to a specific area/department’s programs 2. Assist with recruitment and communications initiatives, including, but not limited to, develop materials for prospective students, students and other stakeholders 3. Create marketing materials to promote the recruitment and retention of students 4. Create photos and videos to promote the university, specific faculties and various audiences 5. Work with stakeholders, administration, alumni, and current students to create profiles for marketing purposes 6. Assist with mail outs, recruitment package assembly, and email reminders to students 7. Maintain presence on Brandon University social media accounts 8. Other relevant duties as assigned Qualifications/Experience: SKILLSET: 1. Ability to work independently and/or with others effectively as part of a team 2. Ability to communicate clearly and effectively using excellent written and verbal communication skills 3. Strong attention to detail, excellent problem solving skills, and self-motivated; excellent computer skills 4. Ability to monitor and update social media presence EDUCATION: 1. Preference given to current Brandon University student; nearing completion of or completion of an undergraduate degree EXPERIENCE: 1. Advanced training and/or specialized experience, plus online marketing and analytics experience 2. Advanced communications experience, especially in video creation and editing is a strong asset 3. Experience maintaining a social media presence in a professional environment is an asset To Apply: To apply, please provide a CV and cover letter to ArtsDean@brandonu.ca by September 17, 2026. Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. If you require an accommodation during any phase of the evaluation process, please advise HR at hr@brandonu.ca. All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. 03.202 Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
