    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/student-assistant-iv-department-of-physics-and-astronomy/": {
      "title": "Student Assistant IV",
      "description": "Student Assistant IV – Department of Physics and Astronomy | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities Student Assistant IV – Department of Physics and Astro… Student Assistant IV – Department of Physics and Astronomy Applications are to be received by: 4:30 p.m. on September 14, 2026 Classification: Student Assistant IV Employee Group: PSAC Job Title: Group Tutor for General Physics Department: Physics and Astronomy Wage: $21.63 per hour Hours of Work: 15 hours Start Date: September 16, 2026 Number of Positions Available: 1 Length of Appointment: until December 11, 2026 Course title and number: 74.151 General Physics I Date Issued: September 3, 2026 Duties: The primary duty is to run group tutor sessions for the students in General Physics I. These sessions will be held approximately weekly, when an assignment or test is coming up, in consultation with your schedule. Tutor will be given the assignment or a practice test in advance. Tutor will assist students in understanding the material, explain concepts, clarify material, answer student questions, offer other support to students and other relevant duties as assigned. Qualifications/Experience: Preference will be given to a student enrolled in the 3rd or 4th year in a physics and astronomy degree at Brandon University, in good standing with a minimum 2.5 GPA. Skillset: Ability to work independently and/or with others effectively. Ability to communicate ideas effectively. Self-motivated. Strong problem solving skills. Attention to detail. Demonstrated patience and ability to relate to students with a wide range of learning styles. Previous tutoring experience is an asset. To Apply: Send a resume and cover letter to Dr. Greg Ballentine showing how you meet these qualifications via email to ballentineg@brandonu.ca Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. If you require an accommodation during any phase of the evaluation process, please advise HR at hr@brandonu.ca. All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
    },
    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/research-assistant-iii-department-of-psychology-8/": {
      "title": "Research Assistant III",
      "description": "Research Assistant III – Department of Psychology | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities Research Assistant III – Department of Psychology Research Assistant III – Department of Psychology Applications are to be received by: 4:30 p.m. on September 20, 2026 Classification: Research Assistant III Employee Group: PSAC Job Title: Research Assistant Department: Psychology Wage: $21.63 per hour Hours of Work: 4 00 hours Start Date: September 28, 2026 Number of Positions Available: 2 Length of Appointment: until March 31, 2027 Date Issued: September 10, 2026 Key Duties: This project is part of a larger SSHRC-funded project on Age-Friendly Communities in Manitoba. Duties for this position will include: assist in preparing research materials; assist with data collection/analysis; assist with preparing presentations and other creative outputs; and maintain communications and outreach to research partners. Tasks will also include other relevant duties, as assigned. Qualifications/Experience: Ability to work well independently with minimal supervision and have excellent organizational skills. Strong abilities in writing and communication. Ideal candidates will be upper-level undergraduates (4th yr +). Experience with communicating information to various audiences via written or visual formats is an asset. Ideally, the candidate will possess strong problem-solving skills and be self-motivated, have the ability to work independently and with others effectively, and have the ability to uphold high standards of confidentiality and research integrity. This project involves working with grandmothers and women (Indigenous and Non-Indigenous); identifying as an Indigenous woman (First Nations, Red River Métis, or Inuk) is an asset. Completion of TCPS-2: CORE ethics. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume, TCPS-2: CORE certificate, and names of two references to Dr. Nancy Newall, newalln@brandonu.ca. We thank you for your interest, only successful candidates will be contacted. Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. If you require an accommodation during any phase of the evaluation process, please advise HR at hr@brandonu.ca. All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
    },
    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/research-assistant-iv-department-of-psychology-3/": {
      "title": "Research Assistant IV",
      "description": "Research Assistant IV – Department of Psychology | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities Research Assistant IV – Department of Psychology Research Assistant IV – Department of Psychology Applications are to be received by: 4:30 p.m. on September 18, 2026 Classification: Research Assistant IV Employee Group: PSAC Job Title: Research Assistant Department: Psychology Wage: $30.17 per hour Hours of Work: 500 hours Start Date: September 28, 2026 Number of Positions Available: 2 Length of Appointment: until March 31, 2027 Date Issued: September 10, 2026 Key Duties: This project is part of a larger SSHRC-funded project on Age-Friendly Communities in Manitoba. Duties for this position will include: 1) Design and Organize special events for Grandmother (Matriarch) gatherings with community partners and University researchers; 2) Collect and manage research data, conduct analysis of research results and document findings; 3) Interpret research findings and perform editorial tasks; 4) Supervise staff; 5) Contribute to overall activities and internal operation related to the project. Tasks will also include other relevant duties, as assigned. Qualifications/Experience: Ability to work well independently with minimal supervision and have excellent organizational skills. Strong abilities in writing and communication. Ideal candidates will:1) Have a Masters degree or be completing a Master degree in a related field (social sciences; health); 2) Have completed research methodology courses at an undergraduate or graduate level; 3) Have extensive organization skills and sound judgment; 4) Have the ability to communicate clearly and effectively. In addition, ideal candidate will possess strong problem-solving skills and be self-motivated, have the ability to work independently and with others effectively, and have the ability to uphold high standards of confidentiality and research integrity. This position requires in-person meetings in Brandon Manitoba. This project involves working with grandmothers and women (Indigenous and Non-Indigenous); identifying as an Indigenous woman (First Nations, Red River Métis, or Inuk) is an asset. Completion of TCPS-2: CORE ethics. To Apply: Send cover letter, resume, TCPS-2: CORE certificate, and names of two references to Dr. Nancy Newall, newalln@brandonu.ca. We thank you for your interest, only successful candidates will be contacted. Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. If you require an accommodation during any phase of the evaluation process, please advise HR at hr@brandonu.ca. All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
    },
