    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/student-assistant-iii-writing-skills-peer-tutor/": {
      "title": "Student Assistant III",
      "description": "Student Assistant III – Writing Skills Peer Tutor **Reposting** | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities Student Assistant III – Writing Skills Peer Tutor **Re… Student Assistant III – Writing Skills Peer Tutor **Reposting** Applications are to be received by: 4:30 p.m. on September 14, 2026 or until position is filled Classification: Student Assistant III Employee Group: PSAC Job Title: Writing Skills Peer Tutor Department: Student Services Wage: $18.41 / hour Hours of Work: To be determined (afternoons). 4-10 hours per week Start Date: September 21, 2026 Number of Positions Available: 2 Length of Appointment: Sept 21, 2026 – April 9, 2027 Date Issued: September 3, 2026 Duties: – Encourage and provide feedback to students in their writing endeavors – Recognize and promote principles of good university-level writing – Help students to understand the basic structures of essays and other written assignments – Assist students in using citation styles such as APA, MLA, Chicago, and others – and other relevant duties as assigned Qualifications/Experience: – Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with proven essay-writing skills – Available to attend training sessions (dates set collaboratively) – Available to work 2-3 hour afternoon shifts in the library – Comfortable working one-on-one or with small groups of students – Minimum 2.5 GPA with a minimum of 30 credit hours of coursework completed – Preference given to current Brandon University student; nearing completion of or completion of an undergraduate degree is required. To Apply: Please forward resume (CV), cover letter, and writing sample to Dr. Joan Garbutt, Academic Skills Specialist (Writing), Email: garbuttj@brandonu.ca OR Karen Skinner, Academic Skills Specialist (Writing), Email: sk