    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/2026-20-clerk-5-office-assistant-full-time-regular-physical-plant/": {
      "title": "2026 – 20 – Clerk 5, Office Assistant, Full-time, Regular – Physical Plant",
      "description": "2026 – 20 – Clerk 5, Office Assistant, Full-time, Regular – Physical Plant | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities 2026 – 20 – Clerk 5, Office Assistant, Full-time… 2026 – 20 – Clerk 5, Office Assistant, Full-time, Regular – Physical Plant Completed resumés and cover letters are accepted by e-mail to hrapplications@brandonu.ca . Please quote the Job Vacancy Number in the email subject line. Applications are to be received by: 4:30 p.m. on September 28, 2026 Job Vacancy Number: 2026 – 20(86) Employee Group: MGEU Classification: Clerk 5, Office Assistant Department: Physical Plant Type of Position: Full-Time, Regular Hours of Work: 35 hours per week Wage or Salary: $29.33 per hour Start Date: November 2, 2026 Probation or Trial Period: Minimum of 6 months to a 12-month maximum Date Issued: September 14, 2026 Duties and Responsibilities: The Office Assistant for Physical Plant is the administrative hub for Physical Plant, coordinating service requests, responding to inquiries, and supporting departmental operations. Responsibilities include assisting with timesheets and payroll documentation, maintaining records and databases, keeping track and ordering office supplies, mail sorting duties, and providing administrative support to staff with work orders, procedures, and related processes. Key responsibilities also include supporting campus security access systems, including card access, door controls, key inventories, coordinating building access and event security requirements, troubleshooting access issues, and communicating campus maintenance, safety, and security concerns. Other relevant duties as assigned. Required Qualifications and Experience: Minimum Grade 12 plus an Office Administration certificate and 3 years’ related experience is required, or a combination of education and experience. The ideal candidate will have a demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities and frequent interruptions while providing exception customer service to both internal and external clients. To be successful in this role, the successful candidate will be a highly motivated, self-starting team player who works effectively with minimal supervision. They will possess strong organizational and multitasking skills and have a demonstrated commitment to delivering exceptional customer service. Proficiency with the Microsoft Office Suite is required. Experience with work order software, such as FAMIS 360, is considered an asset. Familiarity working in a unionized environment would be an asset. *NOTE* Skill based testing will be required. This position is subject to a Child Abuse Registry Check and Criminal Record Check. The successful candidate will be responsible for any service charges incurred. These checks must be submitted in accordance with the Policy in order to maintain employment. Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. Should you require an accommodation during any phase of the recruitment process, contact HR at hr@brandonu.ca . All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
    },
